**How to read the table.** Each row is a different model trained on the same data. "d-4-d" means 19 inputs squeezed through 4 internal units and expanded back to 19 outputs, and the deeper model adds a layer on each side. The PCA rows are the linear equivalent with the same number of components. Lower reconstruction error means normal windows are copied more faithfully. ROC AUC measures how well attacks are ranked above normal windows, from 0.5 (chance) to 1.

**What the table tells you.** Each autoencoder performs much like the PCA of the same size, in error and in detection. Better reconstruction does not mean better detection: the 19-8-19 model reconstructs best but ranks attacks worst of the autoencoders, because it also learns to copy part of the attack signal. The deeper network adds nothing on detection either. We keep the shallow four-unit model and test it against simple baselines on the Evaluation page.
